.TH JJMCP-SECURITY 7 "May 2026" "JJMCP 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
jjmcp-security \- security model for JohnJuliaMCP
.SH DESCRIPTION
JJMCP is a local trusted tool.
It can execute arbitrary Julia code in the tmux pane selected by
.B jjmcp_bind.
.PP
Only expose this MCP server to trusted local clients.
Do not run it as a network service, do not bind it to an untrusted tmux pane, and do not give untrusted agents access to it.
.SH RISKS
.IP \(bu 2
.B jjmcp_eval,
.B jjmcp_test,
.B jjmcp_activate,
and
.B jjmcp_revise
execute code in the user's Julia process.
.IP \(bu 2
Julia code is not sandboxed and runs with the user's permissions.
.IP \(bu 2
The bound pane is shared mutable state.
Manual user input or other automation can affect later evaluations.
.IP \(bu 2
Julia code can read, write, or delete files accessible to the user.
.SH RECOMMENDATION
Use JJMCP only on machines and repositories where local code execution by the connected MCP client is acceptable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jjmcp (1),
.BR jjmcp-config (5)
